# The level 1 tests that must pass (not skip) in the testbed jobs of ci.yml and in the kernel matrix of nightly.yml:
# each job loads this file into its environment (`grep -E '^[A-Z0-9_]+=' .github/level1-tests.env >> "$GITHUB_ENV"`) and
# names the lists with `-expect-pass`, so a renamed or vanished test, or one that skips on a kernel, fails the job
# instead of leaving it green. NAME=comma-separated test names, one line per list; the acceptance maps in
# docs/development.md say what each list covers.

# The level 1 tests of port forwarding (M35a): both testbed jobs name them with -expect-pass, so a renamed or
# vanished test fails the job instead of leaving it green (the acceptance map in docs/development.md).
M35A_LEVEL1=TestAForwardReachesTheListenersOfADeviceOnTheRealKernel,TestAForwardDoesNotCountIPv6ConnectionsToItsEntryInterfaceOnTheRealKernel,TestRulesOnTheTargetDecideForwardedConnectionsOnTheRealKernel,TestACutWindowResetsAnEstablishedForwardedConnectionOnTheRealKernel,TestAForwardFollowsANewEntryAddressAndANewDeviceAddressOnTheRealKernel,TestAForwardPassesDockersForwardPolicyThroughDockerUser,TestForwardsReachTheDeviceFromBothSidesAndFollowItsAddress,TestAForwardFollowsANewUplinkAddress,TestADeviceFaultDoesNotImpairAForwardedConnection,TestARuleOnTheDeviceCutsAnEstablishedForwardedConnection,TestAForwardCountsTheConnectionsAnAllowRuleAcceptsOnTheRealKernel,TestAnAllowAllRuleDoesNotOpenTheManagementNetworkWhileAManagementForwardWorks,TestAManagementForwardAnswersAPeerBehindARouterOfTheManagementNetwork,TestWithoutTheUplinkDefaultAnAllowAllRuleStillDoesNotOpenTheManagementNetwork,TestAMatrixEntryOpensTheManagementNetworkBehindAManagementInterfaceOfItsOwn,TestAMatrixEntryOpensTheManagementNetworkThroughTheUplink,TestAForwardReachesAnIdleDeviceWhoseNeighborEntryIsStale,TestTheRepliesOfAManagementForwardedConnectionStayOffTheUplinkAfterTheForwardIsDeleted,TestTheGuardKeepsADeviceOutOfAManagementRoleWireGuardNetworkUntilAMatrixEntryOpensIt

# The level 1 tests of scenario runs (M15): the steps of a run on the real kernel and the real clock, within 100 ms of
# their schedule where the machine is accurate, an abort and an expired lease that take the run's overlays out.
M15_LEVEL1=TestAScenarioRunsOnTheRealKernelAndItsStepsAreOnTime,TestAnAbortOnTheRealKernelTakesTheOverlaysOfTheRunOut,TestAnExpiredLeaseOnTheRealKernelRemovesTheFault

# The level 1 tests of checks and zero-hit warnings (M16): a scripted device that comes back after a cut or gives up, a
# device that resolves a name or talks to an allowed and a disallowed server, the limit of the traffic checks under a drop, and a
# fault that matches nothing, on the real kernel.
M16_LEVEL1=TestChecksPassForADeviceThatReconnectsOnTheRealKernel,TestChecksFailForADeviceThatDoesNotReconnectOnTheRealKernel,TestAFaultThatNeverMatchesIsAZeroHitWarningOnTheRealKernel,TestTrafficNotSeenWithExceptDecidesOnTheRealKernel,TestDNSQuerySeenDecidesForADeviceOnTheRealKernel,TestTheTrafficChecksDoNotSeeWhatTheGatewayDropsOnTheRealKernel

# The level 1 tests of packet captures (M17): the AF_PACKET sockets of the executor on the loopback interface, the
# executor protocol over its socket (these need CAP_NET_RAW, so they carry the build tag testbed and run in the
# testbed jobs only), and the captures over the API on the real kernel against a capture on the device itself.
M17_LEVEL1=TestACaptureOnTheLoopbackHoldsExactlyTheSelectedTraffic,TestTheSnapLengthCutsPacketsAndKeepsTheOriginalLength,TestACaptureOfThePcapFormatIsReadableAndHasTheLinkType,TestTheSizeLimitEndsTheCaptureAndTheFileStaysWithinIt,TestTheDurationEndsTheCapture,TestACaptureStopsWhenTheDiskIsAlmostFullAndRefusesToStartOnOne,TestARingBufferCaptureKeepsTheNewestPackets,TestAMissingInterfaceAndABadFilterAreRefusedAtTheStart,TestACanceledContextEndsTheCaptureWithAnError,TestAFullDiskIsTheDiskLowReason,TestStopIsIdempotentAndTheFirstReasonStays,TestADeviceCaptureHoldsTheFramesOfItsAddressInBothDirectionsAndNoOthers,TestASelectorCaptureHoldsOnlyTheMatchingTrafficOfTheDevice,TestAFilterTooLargeForTheKernelIsAppliedInUserSpace,TestACaptureStartsStreamsItsCountersAndEndsWhenItIsStopped,TestAStopForTheEndOfARunIsPassedOn,TestOnlyMaxCapturesRunAtOnceAndASlotComesBackWithTheEnd,TestACaptureOnAFullDiskIsRefusedAndStopsWhenTheDiskFills,TestTheFilesOfACaptureBelongToTheOwnerOfItsDirectory,TestACaptureOverTheSocketHasTheSameEventsAndEndsWithAStop,TestAConnectionThatBreaksEndsItsCaptureAndGivesTheSlotBack,TestTheSocketNamesTheReasonsACaptureIsRefused,TestTheSocketRefusesACaptureWithTheErrorAndKeepsServing,TestARedialingClientOpensCapturesToo,TestACaptureOfADeviceIsExactlyTheCaptureOnTheDeviceItselfOnTheRealKernel,TestASelectorCaptureHoldsTheConnectionsItNamesOnTheRealKernel,TestTheUplinkCaptureShowsThePacketsAfterNATOnTheRealKernel,TestAWireGuardNetworkIsCapturedAsRawIPOnTheRealKernel,TestARunWithCaptureTrueAttachesTheTrafficOfItsTargetOnTheRealKernel,TestALowDiskStopsTheCaptureButNotTheRunOnTheRealKernel,TestTheExecutorRefusesACaptureOnAVolumeBelowItsLimitOnTheRealKernel

# The level 1 tests of chaosctl (M18): `with` under a delay on the wire and its cleanup after a failing command, runs from a
# file with the exit codes 0 and 1 against a scripted device, an abort on a signal, `wait device`, and a fault whose
# lease is not renewed, on the real kernel.
M18_LEVEL1=TestChaosctlWithDelaysThePathAndCleansUpAfterAFailingCommandOnTheRealKernel,TestChaosctlRunPassesForADeviceThatReconnectsOnTheRealKernel,TestChaosctlRunFailsForADeviceThatDoesNotReconnectOnTheRealKernel,TestChaosctlAbortsARunOnASignalAndTakesTheFaultOutOnTheRealKernel,TestChaosctlWaitsForADeviceAndItsConnectionOnTheRealKernel,TestAFaultWhoseLeaseIsNotRenewedLeavesTheRealKernelOnItsOwn

# The level 1 tests of Kea's packet socket after a link flap of a test port (#64), named the same way: the testbed
# test and the tests against the real Kea, which run as root only.
I64_LEVEL1=TestDHCPAnswersAgainAfterTheTestPortFlappedDuringAnApply,TestTheHostReadingCountsACarrierFlapOnARealKernel,TestReopenConfiguresKeaAgainWithAnUnchangedConfiguration,TestKeaRetriesASocketItCouldNotOpen

# The older tests against the real Kea (internal/kea/kea_testbed_test.go, startKea; I64-05): they run as root
# only, so they carry the build tag testbed and are named the same way, and a run in which one skips fails. The
# tests against the real Kea without the tag (TestKeaAcceptsTheRenderedConfiguration, and the engine's restart
# test, which runs as root only) are in packages with tagged tests, so the testbed runner builds and runs them too.
KEA_LEVEL1=TestTheClientDrivesARealKea,TestLeasesArePagedPastTheLimit,TestKeaAcceptsTheRenderedConfiguration,TestTheConfigurationIsSentAgainToAKeaThatRestarted

# The level 1 tests of the DHCP test actions (M23): `udhcpc` in the client namespaces against the real Kea in the gateway's namespace observes
# a short lease of a network and of a device (the lease time it is given, and a renewal at half of it), the deletion of leases (the
# client gets the same address at its renewal), force a new IP (the refused renewal, the new address, and the fault of the device
# that stays attached to it), the options of an action and silence. The last six tests of internal/kea talk DHCP to the real Kea
# on the loopback, as a relay agent: the NAK of a moved reservation, the lease class, the class DROP, the options of a reservation
# and the deletion of leases, without a namespace.
M23_LEVEL1=TestAShortLeaseOfTheNetworkIsWhatUdhcpcGetsAndItRenewsSoonOnTheRealKernel,TestAShortLeaseOfADeviceReachesOnlyThatDeviceOnTheRealKernel,TestDeletingTheLeaseRemovesItAndTheClientGetsTheSameAddressAtItsRenewalOnTheRealKernel,TestForceNewIPMovesTheClientAtItsRenewalOnTheRealKernel,TestADeviceFaultStaysAttachedAfterTheForcedNewIPOnTheRealKernel,TestSetOptionsChangeWhatTheClientIsToldOnTheRealKernel,TestSilenceLeavesTheClientWithoutAnAnswerOnTheRealKernel,TestAShortLeaseOfASubnetIsWhatEveryClientGetsEvenOneThatAsksForAnHour,TestALeaseClassGivesItsClientsTheirOwnLeaseTimeAndNoOtherClient,TestAClientThatAsksAgainSoonGetsTheWholeLeaseTimeNotWhatIsLeft,TestSilencedClientsAreNotAnsweredAndTheOthersAre,TestAReservationOfAnotherAddressNaksTheRenewalAndTheClientGetsTheReservedAddress,TestAReservationWithOptionsOnlyChangesTheOptionsOfItsClient,TestDeletingLeasesRemovesThoseOfTheClientsOrTheSubnetAndTheClientGetsTheSameAddressBack

# The level 1 tests of the diagnostics (M24): every type against the reference services of the server namespace over the real wires
# (ping, TCP, UDP, DNS, HTTP, TLS with the certificates of the responder, the path), their failures (a closed port, a host nobody
# answers for, a name that does not exist, an expired certificate), and that the diagnostics of the gateway do not pass through the
# faults of a device.
M24_LEVEL1=TestEveryDiagnosticAgainstTheServerNamespaceOfTheTestbed,TestDiagnosticsFromTheGatewayDoNotPassThroughTheFaultsOfDevices

# The acceptance of issue #79 on the real kernel (issue #92): the observed state of a device with the observation
# wired as the product wires it, a steady rate in every sample of a shaped transfer, no flap of a device that talks
# every 30 s, and an unplugged device with an open TCP connection that goes offline after OfflineAfter.
I79_LEVEL1=TestASteadyTransferShowsASteadyRateInEverySampleOnTheRealKernel,TestADeviceThatTalksEveryThirtySecondsStaysOnlineWithoutFlapsOnTheRealKernel,TestAnUnpluggedDeviceWithAnOpenConnectionGoesOfflineAfterOfflineAfterOnTheRealKernel

# The level 1 tests of the DNS faults and hostname selectors (M20): `dig` from a client shows each fault, the DNS broken profile next
# to a latency fault, a hostname fault that acts on the resolved addresses only and keeps a long-lived connection past a 1 s
# TTL, the set that survives ten overlay changes, a drop rule with a hostname, the redirect of hardcoded resolvers and the
# DoT block, the latency of a device's queries, the set updates beside applies and the answer latency of names in a set, and
# the executor's netlink connection on the real kernel, and a hostname fault that follows its device to the address of a forced
# new IP without a new query (P5-AUDIT-01).
M20_LEVEL1=TestDigFromAClientShowsEachDNSFaultOnTheRealKernel,TestTheDNSBrokenProfileActivatesAndCombinesWithALatencyFaultOnTheRealKernel,TestAHostnameFaultAffectsOnlyTrafficToTheResolvedAddressesOnTheRealKernel,TestALongLivedConnectionKeepsItsHostnameFaultPastAOneSecondTTLOnTheRealKernel,TestTheDNSDerivedSetSurvivesTenOverlayChangesOnTheRealKernel,TestADropRuleWithAHostnameBlocksTheResolvedAddressesOnTheRealKernel,TestHardcodedDNSIsRedirectedAndDoTIsBlockedOnTheRealKernel,TestUploadAndDownloadLatencyApplyToTheQueriesOfADeviceOnTheRealKernel,TestSetUpdatesAreWrittenBesideAppliesOnTheRealKernel,TestTheAddedAnswerLatencyForHostnameSetNamesMeetsThePlanOnTheRealKernel,TestTheNetlinkConnectionWritesAndRefreshesDNSElementsInTheGatewayNamespace,TestADNSElementIsWrittenWhileTheExecutorAppliesALargeTransactionOnTheRealKernel,TestAHostnameFaultStillActsAfterTheForcedNewIPWithoutANewQueryOnTheRealKernel

# The level 1 tests of the TLS responder (M21): a correct client (Python's ssl, `openssl s_client` and `curl`) rejects the
# certificate of every case with TLS 1.2 and 1.3, an insecure one is flagged by the check, what no case decides reaches the real
# server, the handshake cases, the "TLS broken" profile, E11 (an access rule before the redirect), only new connections are
# redirected with cut_existing and the reset on removal, the device's latency on the connections to the responder, a client of a
# WireGuard network, a connection no case decides that reaches a server in another test network and behind a WireGuard client (P5-M21-02), and the redirect inside the service namespace, on the real kernel.
M21_LEVEL1=TestACorrectClientRejectsEveryCertificateCaseWithTLS12And13OnTheRealKernel,TestOpenSSLAndCurlRejectTheCertificatesOfTheCasesOnTheRealKernel,TestADeviceThatTakesTheBrokenCertificateIsFlaggedByTheCheckOnTheRealKernel,TestAConnectionNoCaseDecidesReachesTheRealServerOnTheRealKernel,TestTheHandshakeCasesBreakTheHandshakeOnTheRealKernel,TestTheTLSBrokenProfileResetsTheHandshakeOnTheDefaultPortsOnTheRealKernel,TestE11AnAccessRuleDecidesBeforeTheRedirectOnTheRealKernel,TestOnlyNewConnectionsAreRedirectedAndCutExistingAndRemovalResetOnTheRealKernel,TestUploadAndDownloadLatencyApplyToConnectionsToTheResponderOnTheRealKernel,TestTheSameCasesWorkForAWireGuardClientOnTheRealKernel,TestAConnectionNoCaseDecidesReachesAServerInAnotherTestNetworkAndBehindAWireGuardClientOnTheRealKernel,TestTheServiceNamespaceHoldsTheRedirectToTheResponderOnTheRealKernel

# The tests of the interception proxy (M22). Nine of them are level 1 tests on the real kernel (internal/api/e2e_intercept_test.go): the first five, the three that follow the level 0 tests of the first implementation, and one of M23c further on: a device that
# trusts the test CA sees the modified responses, the delays and a reused connection through the real mitmproxy in the service namespace, block_quic drops
# UDP 443 of the clients of the case, the checks of a run see the proxy's handshakes, the key log decrypts a capture of the real executor, and the
# connections of a case are reset when the proxy is not there; the three: the per-case policy for the servers' certificates (P5-M22-03) over the API,
# a client with a real QUIC stack that falls back to TCP after its UDP 443 is dropped, and a case that reaches a server in another test network and
# behind a WireGuard client (P5-M21-02); the one of M23c: chaosctl makes an interception case and reads its exchanges and the test CA. The others run the real mitmproxy on the loopback
# (internal/tlsresponder/mitm_test.go, mitm_upstream_test.go, mitm_h2abort_test.go, mitm_unknown_test.go, mitm_headers_test.go: the policies, an abort over
# HTTP/2, a connection whose case the proxy does not know, the headers of a modify rule on a status answer) and are listed so that a testbed image
# without mitmproxy cannot skip them.
M22_LEVEL1=TestADeviceTrustingTheTestCASeesTheModifiedResponsesAndDelaysOnTheRealKernel,TestBlockQUICDropsUDP443OfTheClientsOfTheCaseOnTheRealKernel,TestAnInterceptionStepOfARunIsSeenByTheTLSChecksOnTheRealKernel,TestTheKeyLogDecryptsTheCaptureOfARealConnectionOnTheRealKernel,TestWithoutTheProxyTheConnectionsOfTheCaseAreResetOnTheRealKernel,TestADeviceTrustingTheTestCASeesTheModifiedResponses,TestADelayedResponseArrivesAfterTheDelay,TestConnectionReuseAcrossRequestsIsOneHandoverAndManyExchanges,TestTheKeyLogHoldsTheSecretsOfTheDevicesConnection,TestAThrottleRulePacesTheResponseOfTheRequestItMatches,TestAnAbortRuleResetsTheConnectionOfTheDevice,TestAConnectionThatIsNoHTTPIsCountedAndAbortedByAHostRule,TestAWebSocketIsInspectedAndItsHandshakeCanBeBlocked,TestANewTestCAIsUsedByTheProxyAfterItsFilesChange,TestTheRequestHeadersOfAModifyRuleReachTheServer,TestAltSvcOfTheServerLosesItsHTTP3EntriesWhileTheCaseBlocksQUIC,TestDevicesOfTLS12AndTLS13AreInterceptedAndTheirSecretsReachTheGateway,TestAResponseThatNeverEndsReachesTheDeviceWhileTheServerIsStillSending,TestTheUpstreamPolicyOfACaseDecidesWhetherTheProxyAcceptsTheServersCertificateOnTheRealKernel,TestAQUICClientFallsBackToTCPAndIsInterceptedOnTheRealKernel,TestAnInterceptCaseReachesAServerInAnotherTestNetworkAndBehindAWireGuardClientOnTheRealKernel,TestAnAbortRuleOverHTTP2ResetsTheConnectionAndTheRequestsInFlightOnIt,TestAServerWhoseCertificateIsNotValidIsRefusedByDefaultAndServedWithInsecure,TestACaseCanAskForTheBundleWhereTheInstallationNamesACAFile,TestOwnCAIsTheCAFileOfTheInstallationAndNoOtherCA,TestTheInstallationThatVerifiesNothingIsOverriddenByACase,TestOwnCAOfAnInstallationThatVerifiesNothingIsTheCAFileItNames,TestAServerWhoseCertificateIsForAnotherNameIsRefusedUnlessTheCaseSaysInsecure,TestCasesWithDifferentPoliciesAreInForceAtTheSameTime,TestANewPolicyIsInForceForTheNextConnectionWithoutRestartingTheProxy,TestTheKeyLogHoldsTheSecretsOfTheProxysConnectionWhenACaseChangedHowItIsVerified,TestACaseWhoseCAFileCannotBeReadIsRefusedAndNeverServedUnverified,TestChaosctlMakesAnInterceptionCaseAndReadsItsExchangesAndTheCAOnTheRealKernel,TestAConnectionOfACaseTheProxyDoesNotKnowIsRefusedAndNeverReachesTheServer,TestAConnectionWaitsForTheCaseThatTheProxyReceivesAMomentLater,TestTheResponseHeadersOfAModifyRuleAreOnTheAnswerOfAStatusOrBlockRule
